  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday night through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 1231 PM CDT Wed Oct 28 2026\n\nOnce this primary upper trough passes Friday afternoon, a much\nweaker trough moves across for Saturday and then a weak upper\nridge develops for Sunday. This means rain chances will linger\ninto Saturday morning, but indications are that these will be\ncoming to an end from west to east across the area during the day.\nSunday looks dry and a little warmer with more sunshine across the\narea. Another upper trough moves into the Plains and strengthens\ninto a fairly impressive closed low over Oklahoma for mid week,\nbut this placement puts West Central Texas on the southwestern\nedge of the precipitation for mid week. Not going to argue with\nthe low chance POPs (20-40%) across the area, especially given\nuncertainty on just where this system closes off. Several of the\nensemble members show the low closing off farther southwest into\nTexas and that would bring better rain chances for mid week back\ninto the area if that verifies.",
